  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Yemen Education Cannot Wait First Emergency Response</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education Cannot Wait First Emergency Response (ECW FER) in Yemen will support the education response to displacement and climate-affected populations in Yemen. The project will focus on both formal and non-formal education, early childhood or basic or secondary education interventions in 4 governorates which are pre-determined. The project is for 18 months in Internationally Recognized Government (IRG) areas of Yemen. Target population is displaced child and host community children aged 5-17 years. 140,000 children in total (84,000 girls and 56,000 boys, of which 14,000 are children/adolescents with disabilities).</narrative>
  </description>
